# Echoes of Sound 

Echoes of Sound is a modern music-history website designed to explore some of the world's most fascinating instruments — from ancient flutes and primitive drums to classical orchestral masterpieces.

Built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, the project combines a clean black-and-grey aesthetic with interactive card-based design to create an engaging and educational experience for users.

---

## Website Purpose

The goal of this project is to:

- Teach users about musical instruments and their history
- Explore some of the oldest known instruments in human civilization
- Practice front-end web development skills
- Create a visually clean and responsive website layout

---

## Features

- Responsive card-based instrument gallery
- Individual pages for ancient instruments
- Modern dark-themed design
- Smooth hover effects
- Informative descriptions and historical context
- Mobile-friendly layout
- Organized project structure

---

## Technologies Used

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

##  Ancient Instrument Pages

The website contains dedicated pages for:

- Ancient Flutes
- Primitive Drums
- Early Harps
- Greek Lyres

Each page explores:
- Historical origins
- Cultural significance
- Construction and materials
- Influence on modern music

